(FERPA Policy Summary) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act \(FERPA\) is a federal law that protects ) Tj T*
(the privacy of student education records. Key points:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. STUDENT RIGHTS) Tj T*
(   - Right to inspect and review their education records) Tj T*
(   - Right to request amendment of records they believe are inaccurate) Tj T*
(   - Right to consent to disclosure of personally identifiable information) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. STAFF OBLIGATIONS  ) Tj T*
(   - Never display student records where others can see them) Tj T*
(   - Do not discuss student grades or performance in public) Tj T*
(   - Secure physical and digital records at all times) Tj T*
(   - Report any accidental disclosure immediately) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. PERMITTED DISCLOSURES \(without consent\)) Tj T*
(   - To school officials with legitimate educational interest) Tj T*
(   - To other schools where student is transferring) Tj T*
(   - In connection with financial aid) Tj T*
(   - For accreditation purposes) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. VIOLATIONS) Tj T*
(   - May result in loss of federal funding) Tj T*
(   - Staff may face disciplinary action) Tj T*
(   - Institution must notify affected students) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For questions, contact the Registrar or FERPA Compliance Officer.) Tj T*
ET
